course: dictionary
lesson: 7915
title: One word, two jobs: raven
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are spelled the same but do different jobs in a sentence. Raven can be a noun, the name of a big black bird, or an adjective, a word that describes something.
explain: «Ravens have been filmed sliding down snowy roofs again and again.» Here raven names a bird. You can tell because the sentence is about what the bird does, sliding down roofs.
explain: «Her raven hair fell past her shoulders.» Raven tells you about the hair, so it is an adjective. It means shiny black, like the bird's feathers.
fact: A raven is a very large black bird of the crow family, with a deep croaking call and a thick beak.
fact: As an adjective, raven means shiny black, as in «raven-haired» or «as black as a raven».
fact: «Ravens have been filmed sliding down snowy roofs again and again, apparently for fun.»
fact: Ravens are clever: in puzzle tests they do much better than many birds, and they can save a tool to use later.
fact: In Edgar Allan Poe's poem the raven says «Nevermore», and in «Alice» the Hatter asks, «Why is a raven like a writing-desk?»
exercise: «Ravens have been filmed sliding down snowy roofs.» What is a raven in this sentence? | *A large black bird | A small brown mouse | A kind of snowy roof | A shiny black colour
exercise: «Her raven hair shone in the sun.» What does raven mean here? | Long and curly | *Shiny black, describing the hair | Brown, like soil | A large black bird
exercise: «Her raven hair shone in the sun.» Find and copy the word that tells you what colour the hair is. | hair | sun | shone | *raven
test: Carroll's riddle «Why is a raven like a writing-desk?» has an answer. True or false? | *False, Carroll admitted it has no answer, though readers invented answers for fun | True, it is about wood and birds | True, the answer is in the last chapter | False, it is a sum about birds
test: Which sentence is a fact about ravens? | They always live in the sea | *They can save a tool to use later | They are small and sing sweetly | They cannot solve any puzzles
exam: In «The raven hair fell past her shoulders», what does raven describe? | The time of day | The bird on her shoulder | *The colour of her hair | The shoulders
